In article <1991Apr20.191041.12636@cs.mcgill.ca>, storm@cs.mcgill.ca (Marc WANDSCHNEIDER) says:
>
>I have NetHack 3.0j for the PC and want to set it up on a BBS I am running 
>here. 
>
>However, a problem has presented itself in that I don't really want users to
>be able to just hit ! and be able to go mess around with my Hard Drive
>
>Is there a way to disalbe this, or do I have to compile the program again.
>
>If the latter, would it be an easy task to get rid of the shell jumping...?
>
>Any input would be appreciated.
>

Try (within a batch file):

Set Coms=%Comspec%
Set Comspec=
NetHack
Set Comspec=%Coms%
Set Coms=

It removes the pointer to command.com (or whatever). Nethack should give 
an error about not being able to find command.com and return to nethack.

Alterately, you could write a quick program that records the person who is 
attempting this and remove them from the bbs. I did this for a much smaller
program but along the same ideas. So instead of pointing comspec to
nothing, point it to your program.

